I have implemented the **Sonner Toast System** and integrated it globally across Gram:

---

### 1. What Was Built & Registered:

1. **[`ISonnerService`](file:///C:/Users/taufe/Projects/Gram/gram.blazor/Shared/SonnerService.cs)**:
   - Supports all standard variants (`Default`, `Destructive`, `Success`, `Info`, `Warning`).
   - Helpers: `SonnerService.Show(...)`, `SonnerService.Success(...)`, `SonnerService.Error(...)`, `SonnerService.Info(...)`, `SonnerService.Warning(...)`.
   - Auto-dismissing timer (configurable duration, defaults to 4 seconds) + instant close button.

2. **[`<Sonner />`](file:///C:/Users/taufe/Projects/Gram/gram.blazor/Components/ShadCn/Sonner.razor)**:
   - Animated stack matching the ShadCN / Emil Kowalski Sonner design (smooth slide-in animation, popover theme background, stroke icons, dismiss action).
   - Mounted globally in [`MainLayout.razor`](file:///C:/Users/taufe/Projects/Gram/gram.blazor/Layout/MainLayout.razor) — **you do not need to place `<Sonner />` on individual pages; toasts will automatically render on top of any view**.

---

### 2. How to Use Sonner:

```razor
@inject ISonnerService SonnerService

<Button OnClick="ShowDefault">Show Toast</Button>
<Button Variant="destructive" OnClick="ShowDestructive">Destructive</Button>

@code {
    private void ShowDefault()
    {
        SonnerService.Show("Scheduled", "Friday, February 10 at 5:57 PM.");
    }

    private void ShowDestructive()
    {
        SonnerService.Show("Uh oh!", "Something went wrong.", SonnerToastVariant.Destructive);
    }
}
```

---

### 3. Regarding Space & Bundle Optimization:

- **Zero Layout Overhead**: `<Sonner />` uses `position: fixed` and `pointer-events: none` when idle, consuming **0px** of layout space on your pages.
- **Native Implementation**: Because our ShadCN suite is written directly in pure C#/Razor without heavy third-party DLLs or Node.js dependencies, your compiled binary and memory footprint remain minimal and clean.
- **Removing Unused Components**: We keep only the active components you need (`Button`, `Card`, `Sonner`, `Badge`, `Alert`, `Separator`), avoiding bloated libraries.

